Subject: wayland backend: no new mode for a same-size configure

The nested output made a new mode for every configure that carries a size,
focus changes included: each one an output mode change for every client of
kde_output_device_v2 (plasmashell, KScreen).  A configure that keeps the size
and scale keeps the mode.

From the research (virtio-gpu-desktop patches/kwin, 0033 FIX-I), its Wayland
backend half only.  The other half keeps a removed mode's resources, and so
its id, for 10 s: since KWin's kde_output_device_v2 version 26 destroys a
removed mode's resources at once, a client that read the next mode event
before the removal was disconnected ("not a valid new object id ...
mode(n)", plasmashell).  KWin 6.7.5 has version 23, which never destroys
them: no id is reused, nothing to fix.

diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
index 00d97af..1459993 100644
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
@@ -499,6 +499,12 @@ void WaylandOutput::handleConfigure(const QSize &size, XdgShellSurface::States s
 void WaylandOutput::applyConfigure(const QSize &size, quint32 serial)
 {
     m_xdgShellSurface->ackConfigure(serial);
+    // a configure that keeps the size (a focus change) keeps the mode too: a new mode is a mode
+    // change for every client of kde_output_device_v2
+    if (!size.isEmpty() && m_state.currentMode && m_state.scale == m_pendingScale
+        && m_state.currentMode->size() == size * m_pendingScale) {
+        return;
+    }
     if (!size.isEmpty()) {
         auto mode = std::make_shared<OutputMode>(OutputModeline(size * m_pendingScale, m_refreshRate));
 
